Z||000000||Fatal Error||07-29-2001||04:04 AM||||I found an 86 with t-tops for sale. Has 5speed and only 60k miles. The paint looks fairly good, has some crap wheels, and the interior has some minor damage. The engine has a rod bearing going. I belive due to lack of proper maintenance. .. what a shame. Anyhow, my question is they want me to make an offer. What should this car go for? Keep in mind it is going to "at least" need an engine rebuild. Thanks for any info you guys can provide. <BR><P>------------------<BR>-FE<BR>-------------------------<BR>'92 Chevy Silverado<BR>(wishing for 88GT Fiero)<BR>(working on 86GT Fiero)<BR>(Can afford 84 parts car)<BR>:)||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||07-29-2001||04:08 AM||||I'd offer $500-$600 since it has T-Tops.  Anything mechanical is easily fixed, so is the interior.  If the body & frame are nice and straight and the T-Top stuff is intact and in good shape it is a good foundation for you to work with.<P>Is it a V-6 or 4-cyl.?  <P>Offer $500 and see what happens.<P>   <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 07-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||07-29-2001||04:54 AM||||subject said it was a 2m4-guess it still has the 4 cyl in it. I don't know what value the t-tops add to it, but the bad bearing can negate that easily as a bargaining point. Depends what the top end is like,rings,cyl walls,etc. Inspect for rust on the frame and cradle,(Mrgone can clue you in on where to look, I believe he has some expeirence with that). Check the mall section of this forum for something to compare it with. If a shop does all the repair work, it could easily cost 600-1000 parts and labor for a rebuild, unless you know someone that can give you a break. I agree with Mr Fiero, offer $500.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||07-29-2001||12:03 PM||||For $500 you could buy it, cut the roof off and then find another Fiero in better shape for a grand or so and swap roofs.  I don't know what Bob Stieger or Ed Parks charges for labor, but it couldn't be much more than $500-$600??  That's what I'd do if I had the money.  If you need a car to drive right now, I'd wait and try to find one that has no known mechanical problems but doesn't have Ttops.  Just my penny and a half.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
